{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfghXz4yw8FnFVyxfk6Yh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `heavy_tailed_choice_noise_tally_switch`, and the self-check printed `OK`. That check doesn't cover novelty against the other models, convergence (one chain can't give an R-hat) or the 30-minute limit, so admission could still reject it on any of those.\n\n**Hypothesis (decision-rule level, as the brief asked):** most of the time people misjudge a pair only slightly, but now and then they misread it badly (a skipped flip, a miscounted streak). So the chance of picking a sequence rises with how much more random it looks along a Cauchy curve (0.5 + atan(d)/π) instead of the usual logistic one. Small differences settle near-ties sharply, but even clear-cut pairs only slowly approach full agreement.\n\n**The evidence is kept simple and shared by everyone**, matching the simplest current models:\n- how close each sequence's running heads-minus-tails tally span is to an expected span;\n- how close its switching rate is to an ideal rate;\n- plus a personal left/right lean (one value per participant, with 400 slots for new participants).\n\nThis differs from the models already tried:\n- **Indifference band** (`shared_indifference_band_tally_switch`): flattens the curve near zero.\n- **Lapse models**: mix every choice with a fixed share of coin flips.\n- **This model**: is steep near zero and approaches 0 and 1 slowly as the difference grows.\n\n**Smoke fit (100 draws, 1 chain):**\n- **ELPD-LOO:** −4362.7, far behind the best model (−3266.1). That is expected with such simple evidence, so it is unlikely to compete.\n- **PSIS-LOO reliability:** flagged as unreliable here, with 2.2% of trials having Pareto k > 0.5 against a 1% tolerance. The full fit may show the same.\n- **Speed:** sampling took 94 s for 200 iterations, compilation included, so the full fit should finish within the 30-minute limit, though I haven't confirmed that.\n\nIt also doesn't address the critique's two discrepancies: neither survives the FDR correction, and both are about the evidence, not the decision rule.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72757,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":72757,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21b00722-4734-4af2-b5c7-d26398c1631b","uuid":"c1f06790-429b-4996-b3ba-d652fced76e4","timestamp":"2026-10-04T06:10:19.814Z","request_id":"req_011CfghXy6hUXEzVtoiqxLVy"}
